## Original Content
Berlin entend doter son armée d’un arsenal de frappe à longue portée pour faire face à la menace russe aux frontières de l’Otan, selon des documents secret défense consultés par le média américain Politico.

## Summary
Germany plans to invest 12 billion euros to develop long-range strike capabilities, including cruise missiles and hypersonic gliders, to deter Russia and secure NATO borders. The information is based on secret defense documents reported by Politico.

## Key Points
- Germany is allocating 12 billion euros for defense enhancements.
- The plan features cruise missiles and hypersonic gliders with a range exceeding 2000 kilometers.
- The primary goal is to deter Russian threats at NATO borders.
- Details are sourced from secret defense documents.
- The report was published by the American media outlet Politico.


